{"title":"Career Roadmap · International Relations Executive","role":"International Relations Executive","summary":"An International Relations Executive supports organisations in managing relationships with foreign institutions, governments, international organisations, diplomatic missions, partners and other global stakeholders.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An International Relations Executive supports organisations in managing relationships with foreign institutions, governments, international organisations, diplomatic missions, partners and other global stakeholders."},{"type":"p","text":"The role can involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International partnerships"},{"text":"Diplomatic and geopolitical research"},{"text":"Foreign-policy analysis"},{"text":"International programme coordination"},{"text":"Cross-border communications"},{"text":"Government and institutional relations"},{"text":"International events and delegations"},{"text":"Country and market research"},{"text":"Multilateral engagement"},{"text":"International development"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A BA in International Studies / Diplomacy is directly relevant. However, the title International Relations Executive is broad and can represent different functions across government, NGOs, universities, corporations, think tanks and international organisations."},{"type":"p","text":"For senior policy, diplomatic and international-affairs positions, a master's degree and substantial professional experience can significantly strengthen progression."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus","Expected Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Foundation & Global Exposure"},{"text":"BA + international affairs knowledge + language + research + internships"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"International Relations Professional"},{"text":"International Relations Executive, Programme Associate, Research Associate"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"International Affairs Manager, Country/Regional Analyst, International Programme Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Leadership & Advisory"},{"text":"International Relations Lead, Diplomatic Affairs Advisor, Regional Director, Global Partnerships Head"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During BA","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student should build seven core capabilities."},{"type":"h","text":"1. International relations"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International relations theory"},{"text":"Realism"},{"text":"Liberalism"},{"text":"Constructivism"},{"text":"Foreign policy"},{"text":"Diplomacy"},{"text":"International security"},{"text":"International political economy"},{"text":"Geopolitics"},{"text":"Global governance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. International institutions"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop working knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"United Nations system"},{"text":"International financial institutions"},{"text":"Regional organisations"},{"text":"International courts"},{"text":"Multilateral organisations"},{"text":"Development institutions"},{"text":"International NGOs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Country and regional expertise"},{"type":"p","text":"Select at least one region for deeper knowledge:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"South Asia"},{"text":"Indo-Pacific"},{"text":"Middle East"},{"text":"Europe"},{"text":"North America"},{"text":"Africa"},{"text":"Latin America"},{"text":"Central Asia"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Policy research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Geopolitical research"},{"text":"Country analysis"},{"text":"Policy research"},{"text":"Literature reviews"},{"text":"Evidence assessment"},{"text":"Intelligence-source evaluation"},{"text":"Policy brief writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diplomatic writing"},{"text":"Formal correspondence"},{"text":"Briefing notes"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Public speaking"},{"text":"Stakeholder communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Foreign language"},{"type":"p","text":"A second foreign language can substantially improve international-facing opportunities."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential options:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"French"},{"text":"Spanish"},{"text":"Arabic"},{"text":"German"},{"text":"Mandarin"},{"text":"Japanese"},{"text":"Korean"},{"text":"Russian"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The language should be selected according to the intended geographic or institutional specialization."},{"type":"h","text":"7. Data and digital skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Research databases"},{"text":"Basic Python/R"},{"text":"GIS fundamentals"}]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Global Affairs Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic focus"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Political science"},{"text":"World history"},{"text":"International organisations"},{"text":"Diplomacy"},{"text":"Comparative politics"},{"text":"International law fundamentals"},{"text":"Economics fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Build global awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"Follow:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Major geopolitical developments"},{"text":"Foreign-policy changes"},{"text":"International economic trends"},{"text":"Global conflicts"},{"text":"Multilateral negotiations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Maintain a weekly international affairs briefing journal."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Diplomacy & Policy Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Foreign policy"},{"text":"Diplomatic practice"},{"text":"International security"},{"text":"International political economy"},{"text":"International law"},{"text":"Regional studies"},{"text":"Development studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy briefs"},{"text":"Country profiles"},{"text":"Risk analysis"},{"text":"Stakeholder mapping"},{"text":"Scenario analysis"},{"text":"Data interpretation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Language"},{"type":"p","text":"Work toward professional proficiency in a foreign language."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Applied International Relations"},{"type":"p","text":"This year should focus on professional readiness."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diplomatic protocol"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"International programme management"},{"text":"Geopolitical risk"},{"text":"International development"},{"text":"Global trade"},{"text":"Cross-cultural communication"},{"text":"International event management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional outputs"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"5–10 policy briefs"},{"text":"3 country profiles"},{"text":"2 geopolitical risk reports"},{"text":"1 international-relations research paper"},{"text":"1 international development project analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Projects"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Bilateral Relations Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"h","text":"India–[Country] Bilateral Relations"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Political relations"},{"text":"Trade"},{"text":"Defence"},{"text":"Technology"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Culture"},{"text":"Diaspora"},{"text":"Strategic interests"},{"text":"Future opportunities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Regional Security Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Study a regional issue such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indo-Pacific security"},{"text":"Maritime security"},{"text":"Border conflicts"},{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Energy security"},{"text":"Migration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — International Organisation Evaluation"},{"type":"p","text":"Evaluate how an international institution addresses a specific global challenge."},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mandate"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Funding"},{"text":"Programmes"},{"text":"Outcomes"},{"text":"Limitations"},{"text":"Reform options"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — International Partnership Plan"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop a professional plan for two institutions/countries to collaborate on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Technology"},{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Climate"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Trade"},{"text":"Cultural exchange"}]},{"type":"h","text":"International Relations Workflow"},{"type":"p","text":"An IR Executive should be able to:"},{"type":"h","text":"Monitor Global Developments"},{"type":"h","text":"Identify Relevant Stakeholders"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Country/Issue"},{"type":"h","text":"Assess Political & Economic Context"},{"type":"h","text":"Analyse Risks & Opportunities"},{"type":"h","text":"Prepare Briefing"},{"type":"h","text":"Coordinate Stakeholders"},{"type":"h","text":"Support Meetings/Negotiations"},{"type":"h","text":"Document Outcomes"},{"type":"h","text":"Track Commitments"},{"type":"h","text":"Report Developments"}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Internships are extremely valuable for this career."},{"type":"h","text":"Think Tanks"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International relations research"},{"text":"Foreign policy"},{"text":"Geopolitics"},{"text":"Security studies"},{"text":"Regional studies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research Intern"},{"text":"Policy Intern"},{"text":"Geopolitical Research Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Embassies & Consulates"},{"type":"p","text":"Where internship programmes are available, target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Political/economic research"},{"text":"Cultural affairs"},{"text":"Public diplomacy"},{"text":"Communications"},{"text":"Administration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"International Organisations"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Programme support"},{"text":"Development"},{"text":"International cooperation"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Communications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"NGOs"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International development"},{"text":"Humanitarian affairs"},{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Human rights"},{"text":"Global health"},{"text":"Climate policy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Universities"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International office"},{"text":"Global partnerships"},{"text":"International student programmes"},{"text":"Research collaborations"}]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The exact title varies significantly by organisation."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible entry positions include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International Relations Executive"},{"text":"International Affairs Executive"},{"text":"International Relations Associate"},{"text":"International Programme Associate"},{"text":"Global Partnerships Associate"},{"text":"Research Associate"},{"text":"Foreign Policy Research Assistant"},{"text":"Geopolitical Research Associate"},{"text":"International Cooperation Associate"},{"text":"Country Programme Associate"},{"text":"International Development Associate"},{"text":"Government Relations Associate"},{"text":"Public Diplomacy Associate"},{"text":"International Projects Coordinator"},{"text":"Global Mobility Coordinator"},{"text":"International Office Executive"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation Options"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Diplomacy & Foreign Policy"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bilateral relations"},{"text":"Multilateral diplomacy"},{"text":"Foreign policy"},{"text":"Diplomatic protocol"},{"text":"International negotiations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a formal Indian diplomatic career, the Indian Foreign Service route is through the applicable UPSC Civil Services process, rather than simply obtaining a BA in International Studies."},{"type":"h","text":"2. Geopolitical Risk"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Political risk"},{"text":"Country risk"},{"text":"Conflict"},{"text":"Security"},{"text":"Trade disruptions"},{"text":"Energy security"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential employers include consulting, risk intelligence and multinational organisations."},{"type":"h","text":"3. International Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["International Relations","Development Studies","Economics","M&E"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Poverty"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Health"},{"text":"Gender"},{"text":"Climate"},{"text":"Sustainable development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Global Partnerships"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Institutional partnerships"},{"text":"University collaborations"},{"text":"Corporate international relations"},{"text":"MoUs"},{"text":"International delegations"},{"text":"Cross-border projects"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly aligned with the International Relations Executive title."},{"type":"h","text":"5. International Trade & Economic Relations"},{"type":"p","text":"Add:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Trade policy"},{"text":"WTO-related concepts"},{"text":"Supply chains"},{"text":"Foreign investment"},{"text":"Market analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International Business Relations Associate"},{"text":"Trade Policy Associate"},{"text":"Economic Affairs Research Associate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Public Diplomacy"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strategic communication"},{"text":"Cultural diplomacy"},{"text":"International media"},{"text":"Digital diplomacy"},{"text":"Country branding"},{"text":"Public engagement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer Type","Key Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Government"},{"text":"Diplomacy + policy + administration"}],[{"text":"Embassies/Consulates"},{"text":"Language + protocol + research"}],[{"text":"Think Tanks"},{"text":"Research + geopolitical analysis"}],[{"text":"International Organisations"},{"text":"Policy + programme management"}],[{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Development + international affairs"}],[{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Global partnerships + communication"}],[{"text":"Multinational Companies"},{"text":"International business + stakeholder management"}],[{"text":"Consulting Firms"},{"text":"Research + risk + presentation"}],[{"text":"International Trade Bodies"},{"text":"Economics + trade + policy"}],[{"text":"Foundations"},{"text":"Programme management + international development"}],[{"text":"Media/Research Organisations"},{"text":"Geopolitics + writing + communication"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Diplomacy"},{"text":"Geopolitics"},{"text":"International security"},{"text":"International development"},{"text":"International law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Project management"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Strategic communication"},{"text":"Diplomatic protocol"},{"text":"Cross-cultural communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Python/R"},{"text":"GIS"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Languages"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritise formal proficiency certification when relevant."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong language credential can be more useful than collecting numerous unrelated certificates."},{"type":"h","text":"Higher Education Pathways"},{"type":"h","text":"Path 1 — MA International Relations"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","MA International Relations","International Affairs/Policy"]},{"type":"p","text":"One of the most direct academic routes."},{"type":"h","text":"Path 2 — MA International Studies"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","MA International Studies","Global Affairs/Research"]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International organisations"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Foreign policy"},{"text":"Global governance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Path 3 — International Law"},{"type":"h","text":"BA → Law/International Law specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treaties"},{"text":"International organisations"},{"text":"Human rights"},{"text":"Trade"},{"text":"International legal research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Specific legal careers require the applicable law qualification."},{"type":"h","text":"Path 4 — International Development"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","MA Development Studies","International Development"]},{"type":"p","text":"Strong for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Development institutions"},{"text":"International programmes"},{"text":"Policy research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Path 5 — Public Policy"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","MPP/MPA/Public Policy","Policy & Government Affairs"]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government relations"},{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"International policy"},{"text":"Regulatory affairs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Government & Diplomatic Route"},{"type":"p","text":"There are several distinct paths."},{"type":"h","text":"Indian Foreign Service"},{"type":"flow","items":["Graduation","applicable UPSC Civil Services Examination","Indian Foreign Service"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is the formal diplomatic career route within India's civil services."},{"type":"h","text":"Government Policy Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible work across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ministries"},{"text":"Government departments"},{"text":"Policy institutions"},{"text":"International cooperation divisions"},{"text":"Trade and economic affairs"},{"text":"External relations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important distinction"},{"type":"p","text":"An International Relations Executive in a company or NGO is not equivalent to a diplomat. Diplomatic positions have specific government recruitment and eligibility processes."},{"type":"h","text":"International Organisation Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Development studies"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Policy research"},{"text":"M&E"},{"text":"Project management"},{"text":"Foreign languages"},{"text":"Data analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Career progression can be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Intern","Programme Assistant","Programme Associate","Programme Analyst","International Affairs/Policy Specialist","Programme Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"AI & Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"International-relations professionals increasingly need digital research capabilities."},{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Monitoring global news"},{"text":"Document analysis"},{"text":"Treaty comparison"},{"text":"Policy summarisation"},{"text":"Country-risk research"},{"text":"Multilingual research"},{"text":"Stakeholder mapping"},{"text":"Scenario analysis"},{"text":"International datasets"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But analysts must verify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sources"},{"text":"Dates"},{"text":"Political claims"},{"text":"Bias"},{"text":"Context"},{"text":"Primary documents"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging specialisation"},{"type":"h","text":"International Relations + AI Governance"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential topics:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI diplomacy"},{"text":"Global AI regulation"},{"text":"Technology competition"},{"text":"Digital sovereignty"},{"text":"Cyber diplomacy"},{"text":"AI safety governance"},{"text":"Cross-border data governance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This can become a strong future-oriented specialisation."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Technology Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","PowerPoint","Research Databases","Advanced Writing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Analytical"},{"type":"flow","items":["Power BI","Statistics","Python/R","GIS"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic databases"},{"text":"Government datasets"},{"text":"International organisation databases"},{"text":"Geopolitical research platforms"},{"text":"Policy-monitoring tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"flow","items":["AI research tools","data analysis","scenario modelling"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Position"],"rows":[[{"text":"BA"},{"text":"International Affairs Intern"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"International Relations Associate / Programme Associate"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"International Relations Executive / Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior International Affairs Specialist"}],[{"text":"8–12 years"},{"text":"International Relations Manager / Regional Lead"}],[{"text":"12+ years"},{"text":"Director of International Relations / Global Partnerships Head / Senior Advisor"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"IR + world politics + international institutions"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Foreign policy + diplomacy + research + foreign language"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Geopolitics + negotiation + project management + internship"}],[{"text":"Graduation"},{"text":"Policy portfolio + international experience + language proficiency"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Research/Programme/International Affairs Associate"}],[{"text":"2–5 Years"},{"text":"International Relations Executive / Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"5–8 Years"},{"text":"Senior Specialist / Manager"}],[{"text":"8–12 Years"},{"text":"Regional/International Relations Lead"}],[{"text":"12+ Years"},{"text":"Director / Senior Advisor / Global Partnerships Head"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"flow","items":["International Relations","Diplomacy","Geopolitics","Foreign Policy","International Organisations","Country Analysis","Policy Research","Policy Writing","Foreign Language","Negotiation","International Project Management","Data Analysis","Cross-Cultural Communication","AI-Assisted Research"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"For this degree, the strongest positioning is an international-affairs professional who combines geopolitical knowledge with practical research, stakeholder management, foreign-language capability and project coordination. The BA provides the foundation, but internships and demonstrable policy work are essential for entering competitive international-relations roles. For higher-level policy and diplomatic careers, a relevant master's degree is often valuable, while formal diplomatic careers such as India's Foreign Service follow specific government recruitment pathways rather than a direct degree-to-job route."}]}]}